{"availability":"available","full":"jacgit18/iron-log","name":"iron-log","description":"Workout tracker: weekly training board, A/B program rotation, phase-based targets, hold/rest timers and a muscle map. Plain HTML/CSS/JS.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-26T22:39:52Z","updated":"2026-10-10T02:25:08Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://jacgit18.github.io/iron-log/","topics":["fitness","github-pages","kanban","strength-training","vanilla-javascript","workout-tracker"],"demo":"https://jacgit18.github.io/iron-log/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:22.153Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:22.153Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:22.153Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:04:22.153Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Iron Log is a single-page workout tracker built around a weekly board. It runs two training programs (A and B) on a rotation schedule, sets targets for each exercise by training phase, and shows which muscles a program trains.","It's a React app built with Vite. You can install it on your phone or computer like any other app, and it works with no connection. It was built and tested against WCAG 2.2 at level AAA."],"features":["Weekly board. One column per training day (Sunday to Saturday week). You can check off exercises one at a time or a whole day at once. In a superset each exercise has its own checkbox and counts on its own; an either/or…","Stretches. On the Board tab, next to Workout, a daily stretch routine laid out like the workout week (same in every mode and program): one column per day, grouped cards you tick off, a days-complete count, and its own…","Supplements. A water log: tap a cup or bottle size (8 oz to a half gallon) or type an amount, against a daily goal, with the last 7 days. Mark a hot day (+16 oz) or enter training minutes (+12 oz per 30) to raise that…","Experiments. Keep exercises you want to try in a list under the board, and add one to any day of the week you're viewing. It's a normal card for that week only; your program doesn't change.","Add exercise and details. Each day has a + Add exercise button; it opens the same add sheet as the Program tab, so you pick Primary or Accessory, the section (Regular, Supersets, Plyometric or Home), single, superset or…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jacgit18/iron-log/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a18993030bb87b6b6ed2d3b58c3212cef892dcdc10f122a7aa24fe42e511fa8e","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:22.244Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:22.244Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Iron Log is a single-page workout tracker built around a weekly board. It runs two training programs (A and B) on a rotation schedule, sets targets for each exercise by training phase, and shows which muscles a program trains.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jacgit18/iron-log/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"It needs a fine-grained personal access token with Contents: Read and write on that one repository, pasted in once per device; the token stays in that browser and is never written into a backup.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jacgit18/iron-log/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"a18993030bb87b6b6ed2d3b58c3212cef892dcdc10f122a7aa24fe42e511fa8e","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jacgit18/iron-log/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:22.245Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-10T02:25:08Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jacgit18/iron-log/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:22.248Z","hash":"a18993030bb87b6b6ed2d3b58c3212cef892dcdc10f122a7aa24fe42e511fa8e","originalBytes":19867,"storedBytes":19867,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["day","one","program","exercise","week","src","app","muscle","data","every","logged","card","github","phase","setti